From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-08-21
Subject: [PATCH 8/19] basicswap: accept a host-managed XMR main wallet's
 identity, receive its config, and guard its fund-moving calls

C9 points the engine's MAIN Monero wallet at the host's own monero-wallet-rpc
(PWNDA-PATCH-5). Three upstream places assumed the main wallet is always the
engine's own; this wallet is DELIBERATELY not derived from the swap seed, on
purpose, verified by the host on its own side before mainwalletrpc* is ever
written.

1. initialiseWallet (basicswap.py) builds self.coin_clients[coin] -- what
   XMRInterface.__init__ actually receives -- as an explicit ALLOWLIST copy
   from the raw config, one key at a time. mainwalletrpcport/mainwalletrpchost/
   mainwalletrpcauth are not upstream keys, so without this hunk they are
   silently dropped between a correctly-written basicswap.json and the
   coin_settings dict PWNDA-PATCH-5's __init__ reads --
   coin_settings.get("mainwalletrpcport") always sees nothing, no matter what
   is actually on disk. Caught live, 2026-08-21: the operator's config had
   every key right, and the running engine still tried to open its own local
   wallet file. This is the fix -- it belongs next to the ALREADY-CURATED
   walletrpc*/rpcuser/rpcpassword copies a few lines above it in the same
   xmr_based_coins block, which is exactly where the equivalent upstream keys
   already get this treatment.

2. checkWalletSeed (basicswap.py) compares the live main-wallet address
   against a persisted KV, main_wallet_addr_<coin>, that on an existing
   install holds the address of the ENGINE'S OWN former wallet. Under C9 the
   addresses differ by design, so this check would return False --
   and restrict_unknown_seed_wallets defaults TRUE (basicswap.py:605), so
   checkCoinsReady would then raise and refuse EVERY XMR swap, with a
   message about seeds that never names the real cause. Fixed: when
   ci._external_main_wallet is set (the PWNDA-PATCH-5 flag), the check
   refreshes the KV to the wallet's actual (host-owned) address and passes,
   instead of comparing against a KV this configuration was never meant to
   match.

3. publishBLockTx and withdrawCoin (interface/xmr/xmr.py) -- the
   fund-moving calls on the main wallet -- carried no wrong-wallet assertion
   before their transfer/sweep_all calls. publishBLockTx's siblings, findTxB
   and spendBLockTx, got one in upstream commit 10ee0843 ("guard against
   wrong-wallet reads made possible due to the preceding optimization
   commit") right after 740360dc introduced the address-confirm-and-cache
   fast path these calls also depend on -- the fund-moving calls were
   missed. Under upstream's single-owner model that gap is nearly
   unreachable; under C9 it is a live race, because PWNDA-PATCH-5
   deliberately makes openWallet() CONFIRM an external main wallet's address
   rather than re-opening it, while the host independently owns
   open_wallet/close_wallet on that same process. Confirm at T, host
   switches wallets at T+1, spend at T+2 sends FROM the wrong wallet. Fixed
   with the same assertion shape findTxB/spendBLockTx already carry,
   immediately before each fund-moving call.

REVISED 2026-09-03 (Grove expansion master plan, Phase D unit D-Z2): the
original version of this patch guarded publishBLockTx alone. D-Z2, while
verifying (not assuming) that "PATCH-8/PATCH-17's wrong-wallet guard pattern
fails closed for ZEPH the same way it does for XMR/ZANO" -- the exact
inheritance claim this coin's whole design rests on -- built a real
XMRInterface, cached the host wallet's address via one openWallet() call,
then changed the connection's live address (simulating the host switching
wallets after the cache was set) and called withdrawCoin: it sent, in both
branches, no exception. openWallet()'s own _external_main_wallet branch
(PWNDA-PATCH-5, above) confirms and caches ONLY the first time it is called
and returns unconditionally on every call after that -- it never re-verifies
once cached. withdrawCoin calls openWallet() at its own top expecting that
to mean "verified" and gets nothing of the sort past the first call ever
made. This is the SAME gap ZanoInterface's PATCH-17 guard had, and was fixed
for, the same day (see PwndaWalletVault/log.md's "PATCH-17 coverage gap"
entry) -- except PATCH-17's guard was explicitly modeled on THIS patch's
original, publishBLockTx-only shape, so fixing Zano without checking whether
the interface it was copied from had the identical hole left the hole open
on the coin PATCH-17 was modeled on, and (by inheritance, since
ZEPHInterface(XMRInterface) overrides neither openWallet nor withdrawCoin)
on ZEPH too. See PwndaWalletVault/log.md's "xmr.py::withdrawCoin has no
PATCH-8 drift guard" entry (2026-09-03) for the full detection writeup.

Four changes now, all in basicswap/interface/xmr/xmr.py (basicswap.py's two
hunks are unchanged from the original patch):

1. (unchanged) initialiseWallet's mainwalletrpc* allowlist copy, basicswap.py.
2. (unchanged) checkWalletSeed's host-managed-wallet branch, basicswap.py.
3. A new shared method, _confirmMainWalletIdentity: re-reads the connection's
   live address and compares it to self._cached_main_wallet_address (the
   value openWallet's _external_main_wallet branch populates). Any mismatch
   -- INCLUDING "nothing was ever cached" -- raises TemporaryError before the
   caller's fund-moving call is reached. Fails closed. Gated on
   self._external_main_wallet, so a non-Grove embedder with that flag left
   at its default (False) sees no behaviour change from this patch at all.
   Factored out as its own method (rather than inlined per call site, as the
   original version of this patch did) specifically so a future fund-moving
   call added to this file only has to call it, not reimplement it.
4. Three call sites, all immediately before their own
   self.rpc_wallet("transfer"/"sweep_all", ...) call: publishBLockTx (the
   swap settlement leg, as before), and withdrawCoin's two branches
   (sweep-all and plain transfer, newly guarded).

All guarded on ci._external_main_wallet / self._external_main_wallet
(fix 1 on its presence in the raw config, which IS what sets that flag), so
every path is byte-for-byte upstream's when PWNDA-PATCH-5 is inert (no
mainwalletrpcport configured) -- a no-op for every install that hasn't
opted into C9. Refuses on an engine that does not carry PWNDA-PATCH-5 (see
engine_has_patch's XMR_SPLIT_PATCH_FILE gate, unchanged by this patch) --
without it, _external_main_wallet never exists on the interface at all.

Also fixed in the same incident, on the pwnda side and not part of this
diff: mainwalletrpcauth is now written as a 2-element JSON array
[user, pass], not a "user:pass" string -- callrpc_xmr (rpc_xmr.py) does
auth[0]/auth[1], the same tuple shape upstream's own walletrpcauth already
uses, and a joined string would have silently indexed by CHARACTER instead
of by field once fix 1 above let the key through at all. See
src-tauri/src/swap_sidecar.rs's apply_host_xmr_wallet_to_config.

See PwndaWalletVault/wiki/synthesis/c9-xmr-lifecycle-design.md, blockers 2
and 6, and PwndaWalletVault/log.md's 2026-08-21 entries for the original
incident writeup, and the 2026-09-03 entries above for this revision.

